---
/**
 * /senate/responses/ — how the government answered, when it answered.
 *
 * A dynamic route rather than a plain page so that getStaticPaths can return
 * nothing before launch. A page file would be emitted whether or not anything
 * linked to it; this way there is no HTML on the server until LAUNCHED is true.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { closureDetail, responseDoc, history, humanDuration, fmt, formatDate } from "../../lib/data";
import { FORMS, formHref } from "../../lib/forms";
import { LAUNCHED } from "../../lib/launch";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return LAUNCHED ? [{ params: { page: "responses" } }] : [];
}

const c = closureDetail();
const observed = history().filter((p) => p.basis === "observed").at(-1);
const asAt = formatDate(observed?.asAt ?? new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10));
const slowest = c.slowest!;
// The anchor document. Counts come from the dataset, never typed in.
const anchor = responseDoc("15895");
const peakYear = c.byYear.filter((y) => y.closures > 0)
  .reduce((a, b) => (!a || b.share > a.share ? b : a), null as (typeof c.byYear)[number] | null);
---

<Base
  title="How the government answered"
  description="Since mid-2022 the government has closed thousands of committee recommendations with a template sentence that states no position on any of them. This is the count, the pattern, and the documents."
>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Senate committee reports · responses · as at {asAt}</p>
    <p class="figure">{fmt(c.recommendationsClosed)}</p>
    <h1 class="claim">recommendations closed without a position on any of them.</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      A report leaves the register when a response is tabled. It does not follow that the
      report was answered. Across {fmt(c.corpus)} responses tabled since mid-2022,
      {" "}<strong>{fmt(c.proforma)}</strong> disposed of the committee’s recommendations with a
      repeated template sentence and addressed none of them — {fmt(c.recommendationsClosed)}{" "}
      recommendations in all. Not one was accepted, rejected or qualified.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap measure">
    <h2>The slowest response on the Senate’s record</h2>
    <p>
      The Senate select committee’s report <em>{slowest.inquiry}</em> was tabled on
      {" "}{formatDate(slowest.reportTabled)}. The government responded on
      {" "}{formatDate(slowest.responseTabled)} — {fmt(slowest.days)} days later, or
      {" "}{humanDuration(slowest.days)}. It is the longest gap between a report and a
      response anywhere in the Senate’s register.
    </p>
    <p>
      The response runs to {anchor.recommendationsNoted} entries, one for each of the
      committee’s recommendations. Against every one of them it records that the government
      notes the recommendation and that, given the passage of time, a substantive response is
      no longer appropriate — the same sentence, {anchor.templateHits} times.
      {" "}{anchor.acceptances === 0 ? "Nothing is accepted, rejected or qualified." : ""}
      {" "}<a href={anchor.url}>Read it</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap measure">
    <h2>It is not routine practice. It comes in bursts.</h2>
    <p>
      Form-letter closures are not spread evenly across the years. There were none at all in
      the first two years of the corpus, and then two clearing events.
    </p>
    <table class="register narrow">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Year tabled</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Responses</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Form-letter closures</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Share</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {c.byYear.map((y) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{y.year}</td>
            <td class="num">{fmt(y.responses)}</td>
            <td class="num">{fmt(y.closures)}</td>
            <td class="num">{y.closures ? `${(y.share * 100).toFixed(1)}%` : "—"}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      {peakYear && `In ${peakYear.year}, ${(peakYear.share * 100).toFixed(0)} per cent of all government responses tabled were form-letter closures.`}
      {" "}A backlog cleared this way falls just as fast on a chart as one cleared by answering.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap measure">
    <h2>Four ways to answer without answering</h2>
    <p>
      The count above uses one test, and it is a narrow one: a repeated template sentence.
      That is the most conspicuous way of closing a report without answering it, and it is
      not the only way. Three more forms are named below. None is detected automatically,
      each is illustrated by a document anyone can download, and every one of them would be
      counted as a substantive response by the number at the top of this page.
    </p>
    <ol class="forms">
      {FORMS.map((f) => (
        <li>
          <p class="form-name">
            {f.name}
            <span class={f.detected ? "tag on" : "tag"}>{f.detected ? "counted above" : "not counted"}</span>
          </p>
          <p class="form-what">{f.what}</p>
          <p class="note"><a href={formHref(f)}>{f.example}</a> — {f.exampleNote}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p>
      So {fmt(c.proforma)} is a floor. The honest figure for “answered nothing” is higher, and
      reaching it means asking, for every recommendation a committee made, whether the response
      stated a position on it. That work is under way and is not published yet.
      {" "}<a href="/methods#closures">How this is classified, and why the other three are not</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap measure">
    <p class="note">
      Corpus: {fmt(c.corpus)} responses tabled since mid-2022, after excluding
      {" "}{fmt(c.excluded)} documents that answer somebody other than a parliamentary
      committee. Every document, its classification and the exclusion reasons are in the
      {" "}<a href="https://github.com/toohardbasket-lab/toohardbasket">public dataset</a>,
      licensed CC BY 4.0. If you believe a document is misclassified, write to
      {" "}<a href="mailto:corrections@toohardbasket.org.au">corrections@toohardbasket.org.au</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .figure {
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 2rem + 8vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .claim {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.6rem); font-weight: 500;
    max-width: 26ch; margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  h2 { margin-top: 2.75rem; }
  .note { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  table.register { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  table.register td { padding-right: 1rem; }
  table.narrow { max-width: 44rem; }

  ol.forms { list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.4rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; }
  ol.forms li { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  ol.forms p { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; }
  .form-name { font-weight: 600; }
  .form-what { color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.5rem; padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: 2px; vertical-align: 0.1em;
  }
  .tag.on { color: var(--series-1); border-color: var(--series-1); }
</style>
